    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/chat/completions",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "Authorization",
              "value": "Bearer YOUR_GROQ_API_KEY_HERE"
            },
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={\n  \"model\": \"llama-3.3-70b-versatile\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"content\": \"Return only valid JSON. No markdown. No code fences. No explanations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"Create a travel guide for: {{ $json.Location }}.\\n\\nReturn valid JSON with exactly two string fields:\\n{\\n  \\\"generatedHtml\\\": \\\"full standalone HTML document\\\",\\n  \\\"reviewHtml\\\": \\\"compact approval-page HTML fragment\\\"\\n}\\n\\nImportant JSON rules:\\n- Do not return markdown.\\n- Do not wrap the JSON in code fences.\\n- Escape all quotes correctly so the result is valid JSON.\\n- The final response must be parseable by JSON.parse().\\n\\ngeneratedHtml requirements:\\n- Must be a complete standalone HTML document.\\n- Must start with <!DOCTYPE html> and end with </html>.\\n- Must include modern CSS.\\n- Must include exactly 3 attraction cards with realistic images.\\n- Must include recommendations.\\n- Must include a real OpenStreetMap-based map with exactly 3 visible attraction markers.\\n- Do not use Leaflet.\\n- Prefer OpenLayers for the standalone generatedHtml map.\\n- Use OpenLayers CDN CSS and JS if needed.\\n- Markers must be created from real latitude and longitude coordinates.\\n- Each marker must show the attraction name.\\n- The map must automatically fit all 3 markers in view.\\n- Must look good as a standalone browser page.\\n- Use a clean travel landing-page style with cards, spacing, readable typography, and responsive layout.\\n\\nreviewHtml requirements:\\n- This is the version shown inside the n8n Respond / webhook page.\\n- It must be an HTML fragment only.\\n- Do not include <!DOCTYPE html>, <html>, <head>, <body>, or external JavaScript.\\n- Do not use scripts.\\n- Do not use Bootstrap.\\n- Do not use Tailwind.\\n- Do not use Leaflet.\\n- Do not use OpenLayers in reviewHtml.\\n- Do not use source.unsplash.com.\\n- Do not use absolute positioning.\\n- Do not use min-height: 100vh.\\n- Do not use horizontal layouts that can overflow.\\n- Do not create 3 columns in reviewHtml.\\n- The reviewHtml must use a single-column layout so it is not cropped inside the n8n form page.\\n- Use inline styles on the elements.\\n- The wrapper must use: max-width: 100%; width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; overflow: visible;\\n- Each attraction card must use: width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 22px;\\n- Each image must use: width: 100%; max-width: 100%; height: 220px; object-fit: cover; display: block; border-radius: 18px;\\n- Text must be readable, centered where appropriate, and not dense.\\n- Include a title, subtitle, 3 image cards, recommendations, and a map section.\\n- The map section in reviewHtml should use a simple OpenStreetMap iframe with width:100%; height:320px; border:0; border-radius:18px; display:block.\\n- The reviewHtml must display well inside a narrow n8n approval page.\\n\\nImportant map behavior:\\n- OpenStreetMap iframe previews do not reliably show 3 custom markers inside the n8n response page.\\n- Therefore, in reviewHtml, below the map iframe, add a clearly visible section titled Attraction points.\\n- The Attraction points section is mandatory.\\n- It must show exactly 3 point cards, one for each attraction.\\n- Each point card must include the attraction name, latitude, longitude, and a direct Open in OpenStreetMap link.\\n- The OpenStreetMap link format must be: https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=LATITUDE&mlon=LONGITUDE#map=14/LATITUDE/LONGITUDE\\n- Do not manually draw fake pins with CSS.\\n- Do not manually guess pixel positions for markers.\\n- If the reviewHtml iframe cannot show all markers, the Attraction points section below the map acts as the visible coordinate list for the reviewer.\\n\\nFor Israel, use these exact attractions:\\n1. Western Wall, Jerusalem | description: A historic landmark in Jerusalem's Old City. | lat: 31.7767 | lon: 35.2345 | image: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Jerusalem%20Western%20Wall%202017.jpg | OpenStreetMap link: https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=31.7767&mlon=35.2345#map=14/31.7767/35.2345\\n2. Dead Sea | description: A unique desert lake famous for floating and mineral-rich water. | lat: 31.5590 | lon: 35.4732 | image: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Dead%20Sea,%20Israel.jpg | OpenStreetMap link: https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=31.5590&mlon=35.4732#map=14/31.5590/35.4732\\n3. Tel Aviv Beach | description: A Mediterranean beach area with city life, food, and nightlife. | lat: 32.0853 | lon: 34.7818 | image: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/TelAviv%20beach%20from%20sky.jpg | OpenStreetMap link: https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=32.0853&mlon=34.7818#map=14/32.0853/34.7818\\n\\nIf the destination is not Israel:\\n- Choose exactly 3 famous attractions.\\n- Use stable realistic image URLs, preferably Wikimedia Commons Special:FilePath URLs.\\n- Use real approximate coordinates.\\n- For each attraction, create a valid OpenStreetMap link using its latitude and longitude.\\n- In generatedHtml, show the 3 markers on the map using real coordinates.\\n- In reviewHtml, show the map iframe and the Attraction points section with the 3 coordinate links.\\n\\nReviewer comment, if this is a regenerated version:\\n{{ $json.ReviewerComment || 'No reviewer comment was provided.' }}\\n\\nThe reviewHtml should look like a clean vertical travel preview, not a full website squeezed into the form. The generatedHtml should look like a complete polished standalone travel page.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"temperature\": 0.3,\n  \"max_completion_tokens\": 6000,\n  \"response_format\": {\n    \"type\": \"json_object\"\n  }\n}",
        "options": {}
      },
